 "beats": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Private William Cathay had a secret.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "photo",
    "image": "discharge",
    "focus": [
     0.35,
     0.3
    ],
    "zoom": [
     1.3,
     1.4
    ],
    "anchor": [
     0.35,
     0.3
    ]
   },
   "section": "hook",
   "overlays": {
    "hook": "Private William Cathay *had a secret.*"
   },
   "captions": false,
   "speed": 1.45
  },
  {
   "id": "name",
   "text": "William Cathay was a woman, Cathay Williams.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "title",
    "title": "Cathay Williams",
    "sub": "Buffalo Soldier"
   },
   "section": "who"
  },
  {
   "id": "born",
   "text": "She was born enslaved in Missouri. In the Civil War, she cooked and washed for the Union army.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "mccook",
    "caption": "A Union army camp, 1862"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "enlist",
   "text": "In November 1866, women could not enlist. So she enlisted as a man, in the thirty-eighth Infantry, one of the new Black regiments later called the Buffalo Soldiers.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "keogh",
    "caption": "Buffalo Soldiers of the 25th Infantry"
   },
   "section": "story",
   "overlays": {
    "stamp": "1866"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "text": "Why? I wanted to make my own living, she said, and not be dependent on relations or friends.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "title",
    "title": "\"I wanted to make my own living.\"",
    "sub": "Cathay Williams, 1876"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "march",
   "text": "She marched hundreds of miles, to forts in New Mexico. She was in the hospital five times, and no one found out.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "furuins",
    "caption": "Fort Union, New Mexico"
   },
   "section": "twist"
  },
  {
   "id": "found",
   "text": "In 1868, an army surgeon finally did. She was discharged. The paper still called her he.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "discharge",
    "caption": "Her discharge, 14 October 1868"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "pension",
   "text": "Years later, old and sick, she applied for a veteran's pension. Her toes had been amputated. She walked with a crutch.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "pension2",
    "caption": "Her pension file, National Archives"
   },
   "section": "legacy"
  },
  {
   "id": "denied",
   "text": "The claim was rejected. No one knows when she died, or where she is buried.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "pension3",
    "caption": "Her pension file"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "end",
   "text": "She is the only woman known to have served as a Buffalo Soldier.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "photo",
    "image": "buff1890",
    "focus": [
     0.5,
     0.4
    ],
